the tears of a couple who starved and  locked up 12 of their children David and  Louise Turpin were jailed for life after  pleading guilty to years of torture and  abuse in an emotional hearing some of  their children spoke publicly about it  for the first time my parents took my  whole life for me but now I'm taking my  life back I'm in college now and living  independently I love hanging out with my  friends and life is great I believe  everything happens for a reason  life may have been bad but it made me  strong I fought to become the person I  am sometimes I still have nightmares of  things that had happened such as my  siblings being chained up or getting  beaten but that is the past and this is  now  I love both of my parents so much  although it may not have been the best  way of raising us I'm glad that they did  because it made me the person I am today  the horror in the house southeast of Los  Angeles was concealed by a veneer of  normality but inside the children who  ranged in age from 2 to 29 years old  lived in squalor beaten caged and  shackled they were saved by the couple's  17 year old daughter who jumped out of a  window to tell police that some of her  siblings were chained to their beds with  his rings remarry two adults who were  meant to love and protect instead chose  to isolate and neglect  now they insist they're sorry Cordelia  Lynch Sky News Washington
 

